------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. PROPOSED INCREMENT (once studied)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Add BOCL:*STOP-HOOK* (lambda ()) and BOCL:*CONT-HOOK* (lambda ()), exported,
  documented next to the other hooks (documentation.org, Extensions > The REPL).
- A signal-disposition table mapping each handled signal to {abort|stop|cont|
  ignore|interrupt}, with a sane default set (NOT blindly all Term/Core) and a
  way for user code to adjust it.
- Likely a deferred-signal mechanism for the non-fatal signals; keep the
  best-effort in-handler path (GC off, re-entrancy guard, sigaltstack) only for
  the genuine Core faults.
